# default: the arrangement `mux go` builds when a profile names no other one.
# Three panes, each with a job:
#
#   +-------------+-------------+
#   |  yours      |  the agent  |   yours: files, commands, long scrollback
#   +-------------+-------------+   agent: whatever `agent <name>` selects
#   |  scratch (5-10 lines)     |   scratch: short commands, log tails
#   +---------------------------+
#
# The left pane runs NO command on purpose. It is the editor pane, but there is
# no sensible file to open on your behalf, and starting an editor means quitting
# it before you can do anything else. A shell prompt is the useful default; open
# what you want from there.
#
# A layout describes pane ARRANGEMENT only. Identity (name, root) and the theme
# live in a profile, which selects a layout with `layout <name>`.
window  main
pane
pane    agent
bottom  5-10
